# Bulky per-game arena outputs are reproducible intermediate artifacts. The
# durable, never-lost training record lives in latest.json, champion.json,
# ratings.sqlite, history.jsonl, checkpoints/, and the reports — those ARE
# committed. Per-game games.jsonl/snapshots under selfplay_runs/ would explode
# the repo if committed nightly, so they are ignored by default. See
# docs/03-implementation/NIGHTLY_TRAINING.md for how to retain them (Git LFS / S3).
state/selfplay_runs/*
!state/selfplay_runs/.gitkeep

# The repo-level .gitignore ignores any "checkpoints/" dir, but the training
# champion checkpoints are durable state (the historical-champions pool + a
# permanent record) and MUST be committed. Re-include them here.
!state/checkpoints/
!state/checkpoints/**

# SQLite write-ahead-log sidecars (transient; the .sqlite file is the record).
state/ratings.sqlite-wal
state/ratings.sqlite-shm

# Atomic-write temp files (should never persist, but never commit them).
*.tmp
